After an incorrect submission, treat the feedback as falsifying the submitted candidate as a whole. Re-read all input and demos and identify which assumptions may be wrong: output scope/dimensions, panel pairing, value mapping, trigger condition, or exceptional cells. Do not respond with cosmetic variants (for example, switching between a uniform background and that background plus one guessed marker) unless a complete demo-validated rule supports the change.

For divider-separated panels, explicitly test aligned cell-pair mappings across every demo coordinate and account for all output values, including rare exceptions. If the mapping or operation is still ambiguous, request a new demo chosen to distinguish named alternatives; do not spend another submission on an ungrounded guess. Validate the transferred test output's dimensions and all cells before submitting.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544451/attempts/07c41a7601b34a5db818bb4c02b598f2/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-grid-solving-continual/references/post-error-evidence-checkpoint.md"}

